WEBVTT

00:01.721 --> 00:04.563
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.631 --> 00:07.840
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:07.908 --> 00:11.486
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.555 --> 00:14.430
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.497 --> 00:17.873
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.942 --> 00:21.187
♪ lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.254 --> 00:22.790
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:22.858 --> 00:24.230
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.298 --> 00:25.836
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.571 --> 00:37.541
Hey, what are you doing
with my laptop?

00:38.109 --> 00:39.180
Going through
your stuff.

00:39.247 --> 00:41.053
Why are you getting
mapquest directions

00:41.121 --> 00:42.356
To abigail
breslin's house?

00:42.925 --> 00:44.764
I just think she's
a one-of-a-kind spirit,

00:44.831 --> 00:45.901
And I don't want to see
her go down the wrong...

00:45.969 --> 00:48.108
What the hell are you doing
going through my personal stuff?

00:48.176 --> 00:49.682
You should really
clear your history.

00:49.749 --> 00:52.224
I noticed you googled yourself,
you egomaniac.

00:52.291 --> 00:53.660
Whoa, whoa,
th-that wasn't me.

00:53.730 --> 00:55.434
Maybe lois
got on there.
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:55.501 --> 00:57.808
She's fascinated by things
that are going in my life,
oh. Oh, yeah.

00:57.876 --> 00:59.849
And... Fine, I
googled myself, okay?

00:59.917 --> 01:01.555
You got me.
But check this out.

01:01.623 --> 01:03.761
I found a web site
for a group called

01:03.829 --> 01:06.438
The rhode island society
for special literary excellence,

01:06.506 --> 01:09.515
And they happen to have chosen
to read and discuss my book,

01:09.583 --> 01:10.885
<i>Faster than
the speed of love.</i>

01:10.953 --> 01:13.294
See? I knew it was
just a matter of time

01:13.361 --> 01:15.134
Before somebody would
recognize my genius.

01:15.201 --> 01:16.606
Whoa, take it easy.

01:16.674 --> 01:18.979
You're getting a bigger
head than chris matthews.

01:19.047 --> 01:21.321
The economy's in the news today,
and congress is considering

01:21.388 --> 01:22.759
A minimum wage increase.

01:22.827 --> 01:24.733
Live by satellite
to talk about it,

01:24.801 --> 01:26.638
Senator harry reid
in washington.

01:26.708 --> 01:29.080
How about it, senator reid--
is this the right move

01:29.147 --> 01:30.752
During the worst recession
since the 1930s?

01:30.821 --> 01:33.127
Look, if we're gonna get
this economy back on track,

01:33.195 --> 01:35.302
We have to get more money in
the pockets of hard-working

01:35.370 --> 01:37.810
Republicans are saying
this increase is gonna, in fact,
americans who are the backbone

01:37.878 --> 01:40.051
<i>Put more people out of work
and make it harder
of the american economy,</i>

01:40.119 --> 01:42.259
For american employers
to compete
instead of lining the pockets

01:42.327 --> 01:44.533
In the global marketplace.
Of the ultra-rich who are the
people who caused this collapse.

01:44.601 --> 01:46.605
Wouldn't it? Senator,
wouldn't it... Senator...
Chris, if-if I could just...

01:46.673 --> 01:48.746
Senator, let me finish.
Chris? If I could j...
Chris, if I...

01:48.814 --> 01:51.221
My forehead, my rules.

01:51.289 --> 01:52.727
Let's go to los angeles.

01:52.795 --> 01:54.634
<i>Big actor, played the father
in that 70's show,</i>

01:54.701 --> 01:55.670
Kurtwood smith.

01:55.738 --> 01:57.007
How's it going, kurtwood?

01:57.074 --> 01:58.814
Good. Thanks for having me.

02:01.891 --> 02:04.632
Quagmire, it's so awesome
that you could come over
after work today.

02:04.702 --> 02:05.838
I know.
I'm so psyched.

02:05.905 --> 02:06.906
Hey, let's make
some kool aid!

02:06.975 --> 02:09.014
No, we got to wait
for lois to do it.

02:09.082 --> 02:10.855
No, we don't-- I know
how to make kool aid.

02:10.922 --> 02:12.695
No, quagmire!
We're not a'sposed to...

02:12.762 --> 02:13.898
(gasps)

02:13.966 --> 02:16.473
Lois (calling):
I'm home, peter!

02:16.541 --> 02:19.015
Oh, hi, glenn...

02:19.083 --> 02:21.055
Peter, can you
help me with the...

02:21.123 --> 02:23.329
Oh, peter griffin!

02:23.398 --> 02:26.273
Peter, you come out here right
now and clean up this mess!

02:26.340 --> 02:28.581
No! You said I could
have two friends over,

02:28.649 --> 02:30.086
And I didn't--
joe couldn't come!

02:30.154 --> 02:31.791
So I only had
one friend over,

02:31.859 --> 02:33.565
And it was just
me and quagmire,

02:33.632 --> 02:35.605
And I said we could
make kool aid

02:35.673 --> 02:36.841
Instead of the
other friend!

02:36.909 --> 02:38.615
You come out here right now!

02:38.683 --> 02:40.118
Bonnie's way
cooler than you!

02:40.186 --> 02:41.792
Joe has
computer games!

02:45.036 --> 02:46.841
Peter, it took me
a half hour

02:46.910 --> 02:48.715
To clean up
all that kool aid.

02:48.783 --> 02:51.391
I am sick as hell of you
constantly making a mess

02:51.459 --> 02:53.732
Of this house and having
to clean up after you.

02:53.799 --> 02:55.236
So I hired a maid.

02:55.304 --> 02:57.076
What, are you nuts? We don't
have the money for that.

02:57.144 --> 02:59.017
Oh, really? And what about
the peter copter?

02:59.084 --> 03:01.391
Did we not have money
for the peter copter?

03:01.459 --> 03:03.565
Hey, did I say anything
when you bought that iron?

03:03.633 --> 03:05.874
Whatever. I want you
to meet consuela.

03:07.211 --> 03:09.551
Consuela, this is
my husband, peter,

03:09.619 --> 03:11.024
And these are
our children.

03:11.092 --> 03:13.096
Oh. Hello,
mr. Peter.

03:13.166 --> 03:15.370
Hello,
mr. Children.

03:15.439 --> 03:18.080
Consuela's gonna be
our new housekeeper.

03:18.147 --> 03:20.455
Why is she wearing makeup
like she's going out?

03:20.522 --> 03:22.160
Is this "going out" for them?

03:25.539 --> 03:27.879
Hey, where you going
all dressed up?

03:27.947 --> 03:29.084
Oh, nowhere important.

03:29.152 --> 03:30.856
Just this special dinner
in my honor.

03:30.925 --> 03:32.963
It's being thrown
by the rhode island society

03:33.030 --> 03:34.803
For special literary excellence.

03:36.109 --> 03:37.378
What's that?

03:37.446 --> 03:38.985
Nobody said
anything, brian.

03:39.052 --> 03:41.660
Oh, I thought someone just
asked why they're honoring me.

03:41.728 --> 03:43.867
No. Nobody
asked that.
Oh, okay.

03:43.936 --> 03:45.305
I-it's no big deal--
it's actually,

03:45.373 --> 03:47.212
It's just you remember
the book I wrote,

03:47.280 --> 03:48.684
<i>Faster than the
speed of love?</i>

03:48.752 --> 03:50.154
They loved the
book so much,

03:50.222 --> 03:52.329
They want to give me their
most prestigious award.

03:52.397 --> 03:53.432
Mmm.

03:53.500 --> 03:55.138
Look, this is a
really big deal.

03:55.206 --> 03:57.313
It'd be nice to get some
support around here!

03:57.380 --> 03:59.720
Oh, I'm sorry, brian.
That's great news!

03:59.789 --> 04:02.496
(laughs): Yeah, what channel
will the awards ceremony be on?

04:02.564 --> 04:04.303
Oh, are they having
an awards ceremony

04:04.371 --> 04:06.577
For how well you did
the dishes last night?

04:06.645 --> 04:09.420
Ha! You got nothing
going on.

04:14.372 --> 04:15.439
Hi, brian.

04:15.507 --> 04:17.179
I'm kathy from
the book society.

04:17.247 --> 04:18.683
So glad you could come.

04:18.751 --> 04:20.156
Hi there.
Uh, you know,

04:20.224 --> 04:22.130
I wasn't sure I had
the right address.

04:22.197 --> 04:23.500
Pizza parlor, huh?

04:23.567 --> 04:25.775
(chuckles):
Yeah. The group
loves this place.

04:25.842 --> 04:27.982
Oh, hey, this is fine.
I-I like this place.

04:28.050 --> 04:29.655
It's... I'm a...

04:29.723 --> 04:33.066
<i>I'm a pizza dawg.</i>

04:33.133 --> 04:34.973
So, how long have
you been a member

04:35.040 --> 04:37.146
Of the rhode island
society for special
literary excellence?

04:37.215 --> 04:39.856
Oh, no, I'm not a member;
I'm their chaperone.

04:39.924 --> 04:41.526
Chaperone?
Yeah, uh-huh.

04:41.595 --> 04:43.266
We're in that section
right over there.

04:44.874 --> 04:46.543
Hey! There he is!

04:46.611 --> 04:48.083
It's brian griffin!

04:48.151 --> 04:49.253
Damn it, randy!

04:49.321 --> 04:51.160
You just spilled
my juice box!

04:55.275 --> 04:56.611
Oh.

04:56.678 --> 04:58.852
<i>They absolutely
love your book.</i>

04:58.920 --> 05:02.298
The simplistic writing style
is very graspable to them.

05:02.366 --> 05:05.709
Here's your award--
I made it all by myself.

05:05.777 --> 05:06.912
Thanks.

05:06.980 --> 05:09.320
Hey, brian!
Smell my finger!

05:09.388 --> 05:11.728
I-I... I... I already can.

05:17.281 --> 05:20.894
Lois was right--
I'm not a writer, I'm a joke.

05:20.962 --> 05:23.769
I'm one big, fat,
ridiculous joke.

05:23.837 --> 05:26.278
Well, maybe you just didn't
try hard enough, brian.

05:26.346 --> 05:28.152
You know what, father
from "family circus"?

05:28.219 --> 05:30.056
All you do is
judge other people.

05:30.126 --> 05:32.498
Every day in the funnies,
all you do is judge.

05:32.566 --> 05:35.040
Why don't you shut your
(bleep) damn mouth for once

05:35.108 --> 05:37.817
And go home and (bleep)
your wife in the face!

05:37.885 --> 05:39.254
You know what?

05:39.323 --> 05:42.398
That's exactly
what I'm gonna do.

05:46.781 --> 05:49.222
(tires squealing)

05:59.257 --> 06:00.192
(sighs):
Ah, almost home.

06:00.260 --> 06:01.196
Oh, my god!

06:01.264 --> 06:03.671
(tires screech, loud thump)

06:03.739 --> 06:07.015
Oh, please be okay,
please be okay, please be okay.

06:07.082 --> 06:08.454
Oh, thank god!

06:08.522 --> 06:09.991
Okay, you're gonna be okay,
you're gonna be o...

06:10.059 --> 06:11.765
Oh, my god!

06:11.832 --> 06:13.605
(tires squeal)

06:27.384 --> 06:29.591
Oh, my god, yes!

06:29.659 --> 06:31.531
Brian killed a dog!

06:31.599 --> 06:33.572
This is fantastic!

06:33.639 --> 06:35.911
Oh, mr. Swanson is
sleep-dragging again.

06:35.979 --> 06:37.517
I'm flying.

06:37.585 --> 06:39.190
I'm flying!

06:45.571 --> 06:47.912
I clean in here?
Uh, yeah, that's fine.

06:47.979 --> 06:51.424
I'm just reading
the funnies,
so keep it down.

06:51.492 --> 06:54.234
This is a very shocking
"family circus."

06:56.206 --> 06:59.484
<i>Radio announcer:
Es el tiempo
para muchos hornos!</i>

06:59.552 --> 07:01.256
<i>Muchos hornos!
(lively latin horns play)</i>

07:01.324 --> 07:02.728
<i>♪ muchos hornos ♪</i>

07:02.796 --> 07:04.702
(horns playing)

07:04.769 --> 07:06.306
<i>♪ muchos hornos ♪</i>

07:06.374 --> 07:08.113
(horns playing)

07:08.181 --> 07:09.752
<i>♪ muchos hornos ♪</i>

07:09.820 --> 07:11.457
(horns playing)

07:11.526 --> 07:13.564
<i>♪ muchos hornos ♪</i>

07:13.632 --> 07:15.639
<i>♪ ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai ♪
(groans)</i>

07:15.706 --> 07:18.949
<i>♪ ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai,
ai, ai, ai, ai, ai, ai... ♪</i>

07:26.575 --> 07:28.715
(tires screech, dog yelps)

07:33.900 --> 07:35.271
There you are!

07:35.339 --> 07:37.144
Uh, what?!
Well, you're jumpy.

07:37.213 --> 07:39.384
So, did you hear
all that noise last night?

07:39.454 --> 07:41.157
I swear to god,
it sounded like

07:41.225 --> 07:43.766
Somebody had an accident
and maybe somebody got hurt.

07:43.834 --> 07:45.606
What? Wh-what are
you talking about?

07:45.674 --> 07:46.943
Yeah, something
must've gone done.

07:47.012 --> 07:48.515
The cops were
poking around.

07:48.583 --> 07:50.288
What do you mean,
like-like joe?

07:50.356 --> 07:52.463
No. Staties, man,
staties.

07:52.531 --> 07:55.974
I wouldn't be surprised
if there's something
in the paper about it.

08:01.560 --> 08:03.131
Oh, my god!

08:05.274 --> 08:06.876
(line rings)

08:06.944 --> 08:08.283
(gruff voice):
Yeah?
Uh, yes, I'm calling

08:08.350 --> 08:09.922
About the ad in the paper?

08:09.989 --> 08:12.061
You seen my dog?
You callin' about my dog?

08:12.129 --> 08:14.535
He's all I got,
'cause I'm a young street tough,

08:14.604 --> 08:16.409
And my parents
ain't so good to me.

08:16.476 --> 08:18.517
So, have you heard anything?

08:18.585 --> 08:21.159
Did anybody see anything?
Or anybody?

08:21.227 --> 08:22.866
I can see ol' reggie now,

08:22.933 --> 08:24.971
Sittin' there
with a smile on his face,

08:25.040 --> 08:28.183
Listenin' to me talk about how
daddy beats me somethin' fierce.

08:28.251 --> 08:30.691
Okay, so sounds like
no leads, then, right?

08:30.759 --> 08:32.095
Oh, no, no.

08:32.162 --> 08:33.635
Doggy out.
What?

08:33.702 --> 08:35.340
<i>Out. Afuera.
I live here.</i>

08:35.408 --> 08:36.878
<i>No, no. Afuera.</i>

08:36.946 --> 08:37.849
But, look,
I'm trying...

08:37.917 --> 08:39.252
Aah! (grunts)

08:39.321 --> 08:40.792
<i>Вїhola?</i>

08:40.860 --> 08:42.396
Stewie:
Yes, could you please
put brian back on?

08:42.463 --> 08:45.943
<i>No, no. Do... Doggy afuera.</i>

08:46.010 --> 08:47.179
You're the new housekeeper,
aren't you?

08:47.247 --> 08:48.418
<i>Si.</i>

08:48.485 --> 08:49.921
Listen, I don't want
to point fingers,

08:49.989 --> 08:52.163
But I'm missing about a thousand
dollars in play money.

08:52.230 --> 08:53.301
I take.

08:53.369 --> 08:54.738
Wha-what... You-you took it?

08:54.806 --> 08:55.709
<i>Si.</i>

08:55.776 --> 08:56.845
Well, give it back!

08:56.913 --> 08:58.953
Come get, bitch.

09:00.524 --> 09:03.301
Hey, brian, you want to see
what I drew in arts and crafts

09:03.369 --> 09:04.772
At day care?

09:04.840 --> 09:06.779
This is called
"happy sun."

09:06.847 --> 09:09.254
This one's called
"silly space man."

09:09.322 --> 09:11.161
See? 'cause he's
in the forest.

09:11.229 --> 09:15.674
And this one I call
"alive dog burying dead dog."

09:15.742 --> 09:17.013
This is a photograph!

09:17.081 --> 09:18.016
Oh, is it?

09:18.084 --> 09:19.288
Wait a minute.

09:19.356 --> 09:21.328
You saw the
whole thing?
Yes, indeed.

09:21.396 --> 09:23.669
(laughs): Oh, boy, have I
been having some fun

09:23.738 --> 09:25.274
At your expense,
old man!

09:25.341 --> 09:26.980
How could you
do that to me?

09:27.048 --> 09:29.856
Do you have any idea how
upset I am about all this?

09:29.924 --> 09:31.763
I killed one of my
own kind, stewie.

09:31.831 --> 09:33.871
How would you feel if
you killed a baby?

09:33.939 --> 09:35.876
Well, I've killed seven,
but the point is,

09:35.944 --> 09:38.787
You might feel better
if you just confess
to what you've done.

09:38.855 --> 09:41.463
(sighs):
Maybe you're right.

09:46.982 --> 09:50.492
Everyone, I have something
very important to tell you.

09:50.560 --> 09:52.466
Is this about meg's
cervical cancer?

09:52.534 --> 09:53.669
What?!

09:53.737 --> 09:56.144
(laughing):
You always
fall for that!

09:56.212 --> 09:58.218
You can't always
fall for that!

09:58.286 --> 10:00.058
You-you just can't!

10:00.126 --> 10:01.497
Go ahead, brian.

10:01.565 --> 10:02.433
(knock at door)

10:04.808 --> 10:06.614
Hi, joe.
Thanks for coming.

10:08.153 --> 10:09.891
Okay, now
that joe's here,

10:09.960 --> 10:12.366
I can say this
in front of all of you.

10:12.434 --> 10:14.708
Everyone...

10:14.775 --> 10:16.479
I am a criminal.

10:16.547 --> 10:18.586
A few nights ago,
I committed a murder.

10:18.654 --> 10:21.698
Then I buried the body
and even went out of my way

10:21.766 --> 10:23.035
To cover up the evidence.

10:23.103 --> 10:24.340
Oh, my god!

10:24.408 --> 10:26.647
These are very serious
charges, brian.

10:26.714 --> 10:28.420
I know, and that's
why I'm prepared

10:28.488 --> 10:31.597
For you to arrest me
and take me to jail
where I belong.

10:31.665 --> 10:33.369
I just couldn't take
the stress anymore.

10:33.438 --> 10:34.709
I had to come clean.

10:34.777 --> 10:36.916
I mean, the truth is,
I didn't even stop

10:36.984 --> 10:38.854
To find out if
he had an owner.

10:38.922 --> 10:40.394
I just completely...
Wait, wait, owner?

10:40.462 --> 10:42.635
What are you
talking about?
I just told you.

10:42.703 --> 10:44.742
I hit and killed a
dog with my car!

10:46.548 --> 10:48.587
(others laughing)

10:48.656 --> 10:50.027
What?

10:50.095 --> 10:51.865
(laughs):
Brian...
It's a dog!

10:51.933 --> 10:53.437
That's not
a crime!

10:53.505 --> 10:54.540
What do you mean?

10:54.608 --> 10:56.046
Well... I mean,

10:56.114 --> 10:58.388
<i>It's not like
you killed a person.</i>

10:58.455 --> 11:00.963
Or-or even ran over
somebody's mailbox.

11:01.030 --> 11:03.070
Killing a dog
is not a crime?

11:03.138 --> 11:05.880
(laughing):
Of-of course not!

11:05.947 --> 11:07.150
Yeah, especially
for you.

11:07.217 --> 11:08.755
An animal killing
another animal?

11:08.823 --> 11:10.262
That happens
all the time.

11:12.201 --> 11:15.679
Hey, sweet-ass,
last night was fantastic.

11:15.747 --> 11:17.987
Hello? Where'd you go?

11:20.630 --> 11:21.799
(gasps)

11:24.576 --> 11:26.448
(screeches)

11:26.516 --> 11:30.463
Oh. Well, then I guess I
worried for nothing.

11:30.531 --> 11:32.568
Yeah, nobody cares
if a dog gets killed.

11:34.543 --> 11:36.349
I could do it, brian!
I could do it right now!

11:36.416 --> 11:37.921
Nobody would say a thing!

11:37.989 --> 11:40.496
I could blow your brains out
and they'd throw me a parade!

11:40.564 --> 11:42.268
What?
Eh, I'm just screwing
around, brian.

11:42.335 --> 11:43.406
Nobody cares.

11:51.033 --> 11:52.368
Peter, what are you doing?

11:52.436 --> 11:54.008
She's still here, lois.

11:54.076 --> 11:56.149
Wasn't she supposed to leave
like two hours ago?

11:56.216 --> 11:58.724
I thought so. Go ask
her what she's doing.

11:58.792 --> 12:00.429
I'm not asking her.
You go ask her.

12:02.403 --> 12:06.049
Uh, consuela? I thought you
finished cleaning hours ago.

12:06.117 --> 12:07.486
Yeah, what are
you still doing here?

12:07.554 --> 12:09.526
I wait for rain to stop.

12:09.594 --> 12:11.233
It's time for
you to go home.

12:11.301 --> 12:13.474
Is too much rain. I stay.

12:13.541 --> 12:15.012
But it's gonna
rain all night.

12:15.079 --> 12:16.550
I sleep here.

12:16.618 --> 12:18.188
Uh, I don't know about that.

12:18.256 --> 12:19.661
I sleep here.

12:21.970 --> 12:24.209
Can I get some
covers over here?

12:24.277 --> 12:28.189
No. No. You fat
keep you warm.

12:35.080 --> 12:37.020
No, no...

12:46.117 --> 12:48.960
You know, brian, I love it
here at the ice cream shop.

12:49.027 --> 12:51.032
In fact, this is gonna
be my happy place.

12:51.100 --> 12:53.373
If I ever get molested or
raped, this is the place

12:53.441 --> 12:55.147
I'm gonna think of to make
everything all right.

12:55.214 --> 12:56.183
That's great, stewie.

12:56.251 --> 12:57.889
Hey, what's up your fanny?

12:57.957 --> 13:00.765
Nothing. I'm just--
I'm a little bummed
out from the other day.

13:00.833 --> 13:03.942
I just can't believe
our society actually values

13:04.012 --> 13:06.954
The life of a dog less than that
of a human. It's infuriating.

13:07.022 --> 13:09.228
That is infuriating.
Maybe you should go bark

13:09.296 --> 13:11.736
At a tree and chew on
your balls for an hour.

13:11.804 --> 13:13.943
You know, that's the problem.
That's usually the way I'd

13:14.010 --> 13:15.783
Handle this kind of thing,
but not this time.

13:15.851 --> 13:17.355
I mean, look at
that dog over there.

13:17.423 --> 13:19.496
You think he wants to be tied
to that chair,

13:19.564 --> 13:21.871
Waiting in the hot sun while his
owner gets ice cream?

13:21.938 --> 13:24.210
Hell, no! I am gonna
make people see

13:24.280 --> 13:27.356
That an animal's life is just
as important as a human's!

13:28.894 --> 13:32.138
Go, fellow canine,
be free and enjoy life!

13:33.677 --> 13:35.215
(screams) oh, my god!
Help! Help!

13:35.283 --> 13:37.958
It's killing my dog!

13:38.026 --> 13:40.466
(screams)
he's got my neck!

13:40.534 --> 13:45.015
(groaning)

13:45.083 --> 13:47.122
(gunshots)

13:47.190 --> 13:51.436
(sobbing): Oh, my god!
My dog is dead!

13:51.503 --> 13:54.011
Maybe that's why
he was tied up.

13:57.060 --> 14:00.472
Meg, will you take one of these
and pass it down, please?

14:00.540 --> 14:02.847
What's this?
I'm starting a
new advocacy group.

14:02.915 --> 14:05.222
The quahog animal
equal rights league.

14:05.290 --> 14:06.826
Our first meeting
is tomorrow night,

14:06.893 --> 14:08.599
And I'd really
appreciate it if you guys

14:08.667 --> 14:09.971
Would come and
show your support.

14:10.039 --> 14:12.814
Well, of course we will, brian.
We'd be happy to come.

14:12.882 --> 14:14.652
Terrific. See, I thought I'd
start locally,

14:14.720 --> 14:17.261
And then maybe try to merge
with one of the larger groups.

14:17.329 --> 14:20.573
Oh, that's a great idea, brian.
Maybe you could join peta.

14:20.641 --> 14:21.643
Join me for what?

14:21.711 --> 14:23.315
No, peta.
The organization.

14:23.383 --> 14:24.352
What organization?

14:24.419 --> 14:25.724
Peta.
What?

14:25.791 --> 14:27.395
Peta is an acronym, peter.

14:27.463 --> 14:28.700
No, I'm not!
I'm catholic!

14:28.768 --> 14:30.172
Are we really
doing this?

14:30.240 --> 14:33.049
No, peter, I'm just saying,
maybe if this meeting goes well,

14:33.117 --> 14:35.054
Brian could be part
of a peta rally.

14:35.122 --> 14:36.526
Somebody's having
a rally for me now?

14:36.594 --> 14:37.562
No, for peta.

14:37.630 --> 14:39.135
That's me! I'm peter!

14:39.202 --> 14:42.613
I'm not talking about you,
peter! I'm talking about peta!

14:42.681 --> 14:45.121
Somebody better have something
to say to me pretty damn soon,

14:45.189 --> 14:46.962
Or I'm gonna have something
to say to them!

14:47.029 --> 14:49.135
I am very busy!

14:49.203 --> 14:50.775
I think betty white
is in peta.

14:50.843 --> 14:52.747
That doesn't even
make any sense!

14:56.996 --> 14:57.998
(knocking at door)

14:59.705 --> 15:01.076
Oh. Hi, consuela.

15:01.144 --> 15:02.981
Hello, mr. Peter.

15:03.049 --> 15:07.630
No school today, so I
bring my nephew, mikey.

15:07.698 --> 15:09.537
You want to buy
light-up yo-yo?

15:09.605 --> 15:11.712
Well... Kinda.

15:13.318 --> 15:16.127
That's it. Peter, we
have got to get rid of her.

15:16.195 --> 15:18.568
I couldn't agree more.
Just let me see if mikey sells

15:18.636 --> 15:21.311
Those things with batteries or
what the situation is there.

15:23.217 --> 15:26.462
Consuela, I'm sorry.
But this is not working out.

15:26.529 --> 15:28.266
We're asking you to go.

15:28.334 --> 15:31.111
No, I stay. I clean.

15:31.178 --> 15:32.514
You don't understand.
You're fired.

15:32.582 --> 15:34.221
No, I keep job.

15:34.288 --> 15:37.164
Here. Here's $40
if you leave right now.

15:37.232 --> 15:39.204
No. I stay.

15:40.475 --> 15:42.715
God, she's more stubborn
than you are.

15:42.783 --> 15:45.023
Daddy, I want a turn
on the swing set.

15:45.091 --> 15:46.160
No.

15:46.229 --> 15:47.498
But you've gone
for two turns.

15:47.566 --> 15:48.735
Get lost.

15:48.804 --> 15:50.708
It looks like fun,
and I want to do it.

15:50.776 --> 15:53.484
No, I'm doing it.
I'm gonna do a big jump-off.

15:54.690 --> 15:56.730
Aaa! Get mom!

15:56.798 --> 15:58.938
Mom! Mom! Mom!

16:02.617 --> 16:05.124
Good evening, everyone.
I want to thank you all

16:05.192 --> 16:07.131
For joining me at this
very important event.

16:07.199 --> 16:09.873
Animals are treated
as second-class citizens

16:09.941 --> 16:11.680
Everywhere throughout
this nation.

16:11.748 --> 16:15.225
We kill them for food,
we humiliate them as pets,

16:15.293 --> 16:17.734
And we use them for
medical and cosmetic research.

16:17.801 --> 16:19.037
Take a look.

16:19.105 --> 16:22.483
♪ ♪

16:22.550 --> 16:25.593
<i>Narrator:
Ladies and gentlemen, your
animal brethren need your help.</i>

16:25.661 --> 16:27.065
<i>Everywhere they are crying out</i>

16:27.134 --> 16:29.204
<i>In the hopes
that someone will hear.</i>

16:29.272 --> 16:30.944
<i>In cosmetic research labs...</i>

16:32.651 --> 16:34.424
Well, the lipstick
is not bulletproof.

16:34.491 --> 16:36.730
We know that now! For humans!

16:36.798 --> 16:38.436
<i>On veal farms...</i>

16:40.344 --> 16:41.479
(loud grinding)

16:46.664 --> 16:48.269
(cheering)

16:48.337 --> 16:50.845
<i>And in simple american
households...</i>

16:50.912 --> 16:52.718
Okay, barney, I'm
going to work now,

16:52.786 --> 16:56.195
But I'm gonna leave
npr on for you.

16:56.263 --> 16:57.602
Radio announcer:
Good day to you,

16:57.669 --> 16:59.005
<i>And welcome to
all things considered,</i>

16:59.073 --> 17:02.484
A show where we talk very softly
and right into the mic.

17:02.552 --> 17:04.256
Do you hear that?

17:04.323 --> 17:06.263
I'm whispering
right in your ear.

17:06.330 --> 17:08.170
I'm right in your ear.

17:08.237 --> 17:10.244
Buzz, buzz, buzz, buzz, buzz.

17:10.312 --> 17:12.048
(yelping)

17:12.116 --> 17:15.862
<i>Won't you please do
your part to help? Thank you.</i>

17:15.931 --> 17:18.270
Wow. Inspiring stuff.

17:18.338 --> 17:21.180
Now underneath each one of your
chairs you'll find a pamphlet

17:21.248 --> 17:23.755
With a simple list of animal
rights do's and don't's.

17:25.262 --> 17:27.299
Wait a minute, I'm not allowed
to have steak?

17:27.368 --> 17:29.674
Well, no. Steak is made by
killing cattle.

17:29.742 --> 17:31.414
No medical research?

17:31.482 --> 17:34.290
But how are we supposed to find
cures for disease?

17:34.359 --> 17:36.498
Well, there are many more
promising research methods

17:36.566 --> 17:38.505
For curing disease
than animal testing.

17:38.573 --> 17:39.508
Name one.

17:39.576 --> 17:40.612
I want a hamburger.

17:40.681 --> 17:42.083
I have a sudden craving
for quail.

17:42.151 --> 17:43.924
No, no,
you're missing the point.

17:43.991 --> 17:45.964
We've got to change our way of
thinking.

17:46.032 --> 17:48.573
Animals are miracles of
nature, just like humans.

17:48.640 --> 17:50.613
But our society
hasn't figured that out.

17:50.681 --> 17:52.752
Do you know that
in some asian countries

17:52.820 --> 17:54.458
They actually cook and eat dogs?

17:54.526 --> 17:57.067
What?! Oh no!

17:57.135 --> 17:59.041
Are they-- are they good?

17:59.109 --> 18:00.847
Yeah, I wonder
what they taste like.

18:00.915 --> 18:03.490
I would try it... I mean, if
everybody else was.

18:03.558 --> 18:05.428
I'm adventurous.

18:05.496 --> 18:07.267
You know what, you know what?
This is driving me crazy.

18:07.336 --> 18:08.574
I wanna eat a dog now.

18:08.642 --> 18:10.244
I say we eat that one!

18:10.312 --> 18:10.814
What?!

18:10.882 --> 18:11.717
Get him!

18:18.105 --> 18:22.385
(sniffling and sobbing)

18:22.453 --> 18:24.025
What the hell is this?

18:24.093 --> 18:26.534
Nobody gives a damn
about animals!

18:26.601 --> 18:30.145
I just never realized how
little meaning my life had!

18:30.213 --> 18:32.586
Stewie, my life
isn't worth anything!

18:32.655 --> 18:35.964
Oh, come on... Hey...

18:36.032 --> 18:38.675
(sobbing)

18:44.796 --> 18:48.239
Don't worry, rupert. I know how
to get him out of his funk.

18:48.306 --> 18:50.881
Poor bastard's more upset
than I was when I read

18:50.948 --> 18:53.624
<i>Curious george goes to his gym
coach's apartment.</i>

18:53.691 --> 18:57.003
Monkeys aren't supposed to drink
chardonnay! He's tricking you!

18:57.070 --> 18:58.641
Get out of there!

19:01.049 --> 19:05.230
<i>Announcer:
Abogados!  Cinco cinco cinco,
cinco cinco cinco cinco!</i>

19:05.298 --> 19:07.505
<i>Вїaccidente?  Abogados!</i>

19:07.573 --> 19:10.949
<i>Cinco cinco cinco,
cinco cinco cinco cinco!</i>

19:11.016 --> 19:14.328
Uh, consuela, does this rag
smell like chloroform?

19:14.395 --> 19:16.534
No, no, is no--

19:19.547 --> 19:20.648
(doorbell chimes)

19:22.824 --> 19:26.467
I need more lemon pledge.

19:26.535 --> 19:27.572
Okay.

19:30.683 --> 19:31.987
(knocking)

19:33.358 --> 19:34.696
Is this the griffin household?

19:34.765 --> 19:36.034
Yes...

19:36.101 --> 19:38.074
There was a fire at quahog
liquor last night.

19:38.142 --> 19:39.477
No people were killed,

19:39.547 --> 19:41.886
But the burned body of a dog was
found inside.

19:41.954 --> 19:43.893
The tag on the collar
says he lived here.

19:43.961 --> 19:45.165
I'm sorry.

19:45.232 --> 19:48.141
Oh, my god! Brian!

19:48.209 --> 19:50.315
What the hell happened?

19:50.383 --> 19:52.991
Brian's dead!

19:54.395 --> 19:57.339
Hey, come here. Got something
you'll wanna see.

20:02.959 --> 20:05.466
I can't believe
brian's dead.

20:05.534 --> 20:10.683
My best friend in the whole
world... And he's gone.

20:10.751 --> 20:12.992
(sobbing)

20:13.060 --> 20:16.703
You know, peter, I think
he was also my best friend.

20:16.771 --> 20:19.179
He was the smartest
person I knew.

20:19.246 --> 20:21.754
Nothing will ever
be the same again.

20:25.902 --> 20:29.178
Wow. I guess my life
does have meaning.

20:29.246 --> 20:32.892
I never realized how
important I was to this family.

20:32.960 --> 20:35.165
Wait a second. Just to
prove a point to me,

20:35.233 --> 20:38.009
You burned down a liquor store
and murdered a dog?!

20:38.077 --> 20:40.082
Well, a stray.

20:40.150 --> 20:41.420
Thank you.

20:41.488 --> 20:43.461
Well, I guess we should tell
them the truth now.

20:43.529 --> 20:44.931
Well, hold...
Hold on a sec.

20:44.999 --> 20:47.941
We could... Probably let 'em go
for just a few more minutes.

20:48.011 --> 20:52.423
(sobbing)

20:55.367 --> 20:58.545
<i>Hi, we here at family guy want
you to know that we respect</i>

20:58.613 --> 21:00.987
All living beings and assure you
that no animals

21:01.055 --> 21:03.328
Were harmed in
the making of this episode.

21:03.395 --> 21:05.099
But we're about to hurt
the feelings

21:05.167 --> 21:06.706
Of this italian opera singer

21:06.773 --> 21:09.448
By prematurely dropping
the curtain on his performance.

21:09.515 --> 21:11.823
♪ figaro li, figaro la,
figaro mi, figaro... ♪

21:11.824 --> 22:12.824
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru